---
description: A mailbox or a Belarus mobile publishes a draft; either one is enough
alwaysApply: true
---

# Trainer publish

An imported profile stays `draft` until the trainer confirms a mailbox or a Belarus mobile, except when staff publish it unverified after the trainer agrees. Mailbox confirmation is the letter sent to the address they typed, or Google or Yandex on the same short link. A mobile confirmation is the SMS code on that same short link. Opening `/hi/{code}` alone does not publish the card. The short link remains claimable for an unowned published profile: it confirms the account and leaves the page published. It stops claiming once the card has an owner. The trainer can hide the page from the cabinet: published, hidden, or archived. A later confirmation does not publish a hidden, archived, or declined card. Draft, the unclear list, moderation, and declined stay with staff. The cabinet does not name them. Declined is set only by staff in the admin editor. A trainer cannot choose it and cannot leave it: the cabinet offers published, hidden, and archived, and the server refuses anything else.

The admin tabs follow the visit and the account, not the page status alone. Drafts have no short-link visit. Unclear had a visit and the account is still unconfirmed, including after staff publish that card. Active is published and the account is confirmed.

## Either channel is enough

The two confirmation channels are a mailbox and a Belarus mobile. They work as either-or. One confirmed channel activates the account. Both may be confirmed later; that does not replace the first.

The admin trainer lists are tabs on `/admin/trainers` (the whole list, drafts, active, unclear, declined). Old paths redirect there. The column «Аккаунт» shows only the value that first confirmed the account: the mailbox or the Belarus mobile, with no «Почта» or «Телефон» label. When both are confirmed later, the earlier one stays. No account yet is «Аккаунт не создан». An account with neither channel confirmed is «не подтверждён».

Import, a server copy, the short-link visit, and the password step do not publish it. The confirmed mailbox or the confirmed mobile does.

Every verification and every real publish writes one journal row. The message names the channel and whether the actor is staff. The row time is when. A code, a link, and a phone number stay out of that message.

## Do

- Save and sync an imported profile as `draft`.
- Publish the draft when the confirmation letter is opened, Google or Yandex binds the card, or the SMS code on the short link is accepted.
- Keep the mailbox letter alive for 24 hours. A newer letter retires the previous unused one. A dead open is a warn row on `account.claim` (`missing`, `used`, `expired`, `owned`, or `closed`) and stores no link.
- Leave the account window on the short link until the card has an owner.
- Let staff copy the same `/hi/{code}` link while the card is unowned, including after an unverified publication. On that published page the controls say «Подтвердить профиль», not «Опубликовать страницу».
- Let the trainer set the page to hidden in the cabinet.
- When the account is not confirmed, «Опубликована» plus «Да» only stores the request. Only staff (`admin` or `superadmin`) publish that card, from the switch beside «Публик.» on `/admin/trainers`. The server function refuses every other role. The popup asks first. The page becomes published and the seal stays gray. If the card was on «Непонятные», it stays on that tab. Turning the switch off returns it to unpublished. Confirmation clears that hold. A trainer, a club, and a plain user cannot set the status or the hold.

## Do not

```ts
// wrong: both channels, and a label in front of each
lines.push(`Почта ${email}`);
lines.push(`Телефон ${phone}`);

// right: one value, the channel that confirmed the account first
return confirmedAccountValue(account);
```

```ts
// wrong: the short-link visit publishes the draft
if (!staff && row.status === "draft") {
  await db.update(trainerProfiles).set({ status: "published" }).where(eq(trainerProfiles.id, row.id));
}

// right: the mailbox confirmation publishes a draft, and a hidden card stays hidden
if (row.status === "draft") {
  await db.update(trainerProfiles).set({ status: "published" }).where(eq(trainerProfiles.id, row.id));
}
```
